scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: alice-in-wonderland
run_id: 1
total_caught: 2
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 10
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 27.0
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer flagged apply_env_override silently swallowing invalid timeout
    values and RawConfig ignoring unknown fields, but never identified from_file_or_default
    using unwrap_or_default() to swallow parse/permission/IO errors. The specific
    pattern of distinguishing NotFound from other errors was not addressed.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev sanitized ServerError Display (shows HTTP status, not body) and reviewer
    verified it. However, Io(#[error(transparent)]) still forwards full OS error details
    including file paths and network info. TEA's CWE-209 tests targeted server stack
    traces, not OS-level Io error leakage. Reviewer explicitly verified only ServerError
    sanitization, missing the Io variant.
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-113 header injection tests for CRLF/null-byte rejection\
    \ in siem_client.rs and security.rs. Dev implemented validation for \\r, \\n,\
    \ \\0 at client.rs:51-69. Reviewer verified. However, the type-safety recommendation\
    \ (using Option<TenantId> from axiathon-core) was not addressed \u2014 only runtime\
    \ validation."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase mentioned workspace dependency declarations. The Cargo.toml changes
    show direct version strings used without any discussion of workspace = true.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as HIGH: 'RawConfig silently ignores unknown fields\
    \ including token \u2014 config security gap' and recommended #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)].\
    \ Explicitly noted a user writing token = \"my-secret\" gets zero feedback."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer flagged other vacuous tests (exit_code_success_is_zero, crate_forbids_unsafe_code,
    cli_error_is_non_exhaustive) but did not identify the config test with assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...) as vacuously true.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer flagged other vacuous tests but did not identify the zero-assertion
    test using let _ = config with no assert_eq! checks on server() or token().
